From 69c4b7e8f5369a6a6827612c3511d556b0f5322d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:10:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] fix(trace): count pixels that touch at a corner as one
 mark (ADR-392)

Operator change: a 1-px diagonal line is now one mark in every outline
preset. Remove ink specks counts ink that touches only at a corner as one
mark in every trace mode (it did so for Centerline only), so Line Art and
Smooth no longer erase diagonal hairlines as rows of 1-px specks. Where
ink and paper pixels meet only at a corner, the outline walker now joins
whichever colour is scarcer in the 4x4, 6x6 or 8x8 window around that
corner (a full tie joins ink), instead of always keeping the ink apart.
Sharp and Edge Detection therefore trace a diagonal hairline as one
outline, not one square per pixel, and without crack filling (Sharp) a
white diagonal line through ink stays one hole. The rule was written from
potrace's published description of its minority turn policy; no potrace
code was used.

Measured against 85ee406 on the audit corpus: Sharp traces the 12 thin
lines as 12 outlines instead of 38 (IoU 0.740 to 0.746; mean edge error
0.322 to 0.329 px, worse, because each 1-px 30/60 degree line is now one
band). On the noisy star Edge Detection traces 33 outlines instead of 31;
reverting only the walker rule restores 31.

Updated expectations, each the intended fix: the despeckle unit test and
Sharp's fine-marks test now treat a diagonal pair or line as one mark, and
the Centerline connectivity test expects Line Art to agree with Centerline
(12 ink pixels kept) instead of erasing both diagonals.

